source('BrinzanescuMoraru2005','https://aif.centre-mersenne.org/item/AIF_2005__55_5_1659_0.pdf','Published AIF 55(5) (2005),1659–1683; DOI10.5802/aif.2135','§2 quasibundle setup p.1663; complete Lemma2.2/proof pp.1664–1665; Proposition2.3 and proof; principal-bundle/Theta*/<tau>/Pic0 automorphy setup pp.1666–1667',cache/'BrinzanescuMoraru2005_published.pdf','Restrictions of line bundles to a smooth elliptic fibre have degree zero. The proof constructs a finite cyclic cover removing multiple fibres. In the principal-bundle presentation, the positive-degree line Theta and dilation tau describe the surface; Pic0 has base and scalar-automorphy factors.','INT1 takes the same minimal non-Kähler elliptic surface, its cyclic principal cover and reduced fibre; the normalized root chart is w^m=u,s=wh with inverse w=s/h, giving the fibre isogeny. The scalar automorphy restriction has discrete tau^Z kernel, so its connected kernel is the compact base Picard group.','Fresh online primary opening and complete named mathematical context read. The source’s references Br3/Toma and their underlying proofs were not freshly opened or claimed; the paper gives the needed fibre-chart and kernel application explicitly.')
source('Grauert1960D','https://www.numdam.org/item/PMIHES_1960__5__5_0.pdf','Original journal facsimile, IHES5 (1960),5–64, DOI10.1007/BF02684746','§6 Hauptsätze I, II and IIa, p.59, complete printed statements and terminal arguments; §7 setup p.60',cache/'Grauert1960.pdf','Proper direct images are coherent and their local completions agree with inverse limits of the direct images on infinitesimal fibre neighbourhoods.','P362 uses rho from the good surface resolution, S=O_X, J=m_x O_X and its powers. The finite-length R1 stalk equals its completion; the explicitly proved cofinality with O(-nE) and surjective H1 restrictions give the map to H1(E,O_E).','Fresh online record opening plus complete printed page59 and setup read in text and rendered page59. The preceding long coherence induction is not claimed as a fresh full-proof reading.')
source('Grauert1963ErratumD','https://www.numdam.org/item/PMIHES_1963__16__35_0.pdf','Published correction, IHES16 (1963),35–36, DOI10.1007/BF02684291','Both complete printed pages35–36',cache/'Grauert1963.pdf','The correction changes the radius condition and associated arguments and corrects a closed-locus assertion in §7. It does not replace the §6 formal-completion statement used here.','P362 cites the correction with the §6 formal-functions application; no closed exceptional base-change locus is used.','Fresh online primary record opening and both complete correction pages read. No claim of rereading all affected earlier proofs.')
source('GrauertRiemenschneider1970','https://www.math.uni-hamburg.de/home/riemenschneider/OR1970c.pdf','Published Inventiones11 (1970),263–292, DOI10.1007/BF01403182','Satz2.3 p.274 and complete printed proof pp.274–276',cache/'GrauertRiemenschneider1970.pdf','For the projective space and quasi-positive coherent sheaf in the theorem, the positive direct images of the pulled-back sheaf tensored with the resolution canonical bundle vanish.','P362 takes an ample line A on the projective normal cyclic cover X0, rho:X→X0 and its locally free pullback. Projection formula removes A and gives R^i rho_*omega_X=0, exactly the input to the dualized triangle.','Fresh primary PDF opening, extracted complete statement/proof read, and all three printed page images actually read. The preceding Satz2.2 proof is not claimed as freshly read.')
source('StacksProject:0AU3','https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AU3','Stacks Project §48.19, duality properties; opened22Nov2026','Complete listed properties, in particular proper duality (2) and proper comparison (4c)',cache/'Stacks_0AU3.html','The proper duality adjunction identifies the derived Hom of a proper pushforward with the pushforward of the corresponding dualized complex.','P362 applies the proper comparison to O_X0→Rrho_*O_X→M[-1], with X0 Gorenstein of dimension2 and omega[2]; the restriction map on the smooth locus is the receiving canonical-ideal inclusion.','Complete tagged page read; underlying linked proofs were not freshly read. Any SHA identifies the downloaded HTML snapshot only.')
source('StacksProject:0A81','https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A81','Stacks Project §47.18, local duality; opened22Nov2026','Lemma47.18.1, Theorem47.18.3 and Lemma47.18.4, complete statements and printed proofs',cache/'Stacks_0A81.html','Local duality identifies the top Ext of a finite-length module with its Matlis dual, preserving length over the local complex surface ring.','P362 uses the finite-length module M=(R1rho_*O_X)_x and normalized dualizing complex omega_X0[2]; Ext²(M,omega) has the same length pg. This also identifies the local adjunction-ideal colength used in RAT8.','Complete named statements and printed proofs read; no reading of every cited earlier local-duality lemma is claimed. Any SHA identifies the downloaded HTML snapshot.')
source('vanStraten1987','https://download.uni-mainz.de/mathematik/Algebraische%20Geometrie/DvS-Publikationen/DvS_1987_weakly%20normal%20Surface%20Singularities%20and%20their%20improvements.pdf','Author dissertation facsimile, 1987','Complete §2.2.2 proper analytic duality p.60, following §2.2.3–2.2.5 pp.60–61','/workspace/scratch/9fcd229a9ed4/base/S6_PUBLISH_c3_foundations_sources/S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_vanStraten1987.pdf','The stated proper analytic duality isomorphism uses the analytic dualizing complexes and the proper direct image.','INT3 sets the proper map to pi_i:Z_i→T_i, takes O_Zi, and uses both pure-CM dimension-two complexes omega[2]. Rpi_*O=O identifies the two derived Hom terms and yields Rpi_*omega=omega.','Fresh online primary PDF opening; complete printed pp.60–61 read in extracted text and rendered images. The source states this duality with a reference to its underlying theorem; that referenced proof was not freshly read.')
source('MerleTeissier1977','https://www.numdam.org/item/SSS_1976-1977____A16_0.pdf','Seminar facsimile, exp.14, 8 March1977; textpp.1–16, PDF19pages','§2.1 setup, Theorem2.1.1 and full proof, textpp.11–12 (PDF14–15); Remark/Definition2.1.2 and Corollary2.1.3, textp.13 (PDF16)',cache/'MerleTeissier1977.pdf','For the stated isolated Newton-nondegenerate hypersurface, the adjunction ideal is determined by strict interior support after multiplication by all coordinates. Its colength counts strictly positive integral lattice points outside the interior of the Newton polyhedron.','RAT8 proves the exact face polynomials, higher-term bounds and noncompact-face inequality for z³−r in its displayed coordinates. P362 identifies the same adjunction-ideal colength with pg. The only counted point is (1,1,1). RAT6 remains unchanged, with its prior source readings preserved separately.','Fresh online primary opening, download, complete statement/proof and following remark/definition/corollary read in extracted text and all three page images. No fresh Arnold/Steenbrink/Némethi proof credit is claimed for unchanged RAT6.')
